    {"id":"a8f2c6d4e1b30975","type":"file","x":840,"y":-260,"width":300,"height":180,"file":"04-Decisions/Supabase Managed PostgreSQL.md"},
    {"id":"drezivo-tenancy-foundation-006","type":"file","x":1220,"y":0,"width":360,"height":220,"file":"02-Architecture/Tenancy, Onboarding, Clerk, Memberships, and Billing Foundation.md"},
    {"id":"drezivo-api-boundaries-007","type":"file","x":1220,"y":280,"width":360,"height":220,"file":"02-Architecture/API Module Boundaries and Layering.md"},
    {"id":"drezivo-tbf030-bootstrap-008","type":"text","x":1640,"y":0,"width":420,"height":240,"text":"TBF-030\nPOST /api/v1/onboarding/{onboardingId}/start-trial\n\nOne idempotent request records Standard (`starter` v1), then invokes the established bootstrap command. The bootstrap transaction creates the tenant, Main Branch, Owner grant, draft storefront, 14-day trial, audits, and tenant.bootstrapped outbox event.\n\nIdempotency-Key + matching active Clerk organization."},
    {"id":"drezivo-tbf033-lifecycle-009","type":"text","x":1640,"y":300,"width":420,"height":260,"text":"TBF-033\nPilot trial lifecycle and request-time access\n\nThe only sellable plan is Standard (`starter` v1), PHP 300/month, with 1,000 active assets and 10 Front Desk seats.\n\nAccess derives from subscription dates: 14-day trial, then up to 30 days read-only. The storefront is online without bookings/fittings for the first 3 days, then offline. A dated operator extension is allowed.\n\nPayment proof is reviewed by an operator; there is no recurring payment provider or owner-facing plan change."},
    {"id":"drezivo-tbf040-invitations-010","type":"text","x":1640,"y":620,"width":420,"height":280,"text":"TBF-040\nLocal invitation state and safe Owner routes\n\nTenant-owned membership_invitation rows protect recipient email with keyed digest + AES-GCM ciphertext. Pending invitations reserve Front Desk seats until database-time expiry.\n\nOwner-only create/list/resend/cancel routes use tenant idempotency and safe outbox intents; TBF-041 consumes those intents through the worker."},
    {"id":"drezivo-tbf041-dispatch-011","type":"text","x":2140,"y":620,"width":460,"height":300,"text":"TBF-041\nDurable Clerk invitation dispatch\n\nThe outbox worker validates create/resend/cancel payloads, locks the local invitation, resolves the tenant's Clerk organization, and decrypts recipient data only at the provider boundary.\n\nA private dispatch marker makes retries crash-safe; resend revokes prior active provider invitations, cancellation compensates races, and stale versions are no-ops. Lease-token completion/dead-letter writes prevent stale workers from mutating reclaimed rows.\n\nTBF-042 claims invitations; TBF-043 owns membership removal dispatch."},
    {"id":"guest-storefront-proof-flow-012","type":"text","x":2700,"y":0,"width":480,"height":300,"text":"Storefront guest reservations + fittings\n\nEmail is required contact only. No guest OTP or reservation/fitting lifecycle email. Turnstile and per-IP limits protect submissions. Owner/business notices continue.\n\nReservation creation sets a host-only, API-path-scoped HttpOnly cookie (Secure in staging/production; SameSite=Strict). Reservation ID selects the proof page but is not authorization; no capability is returned in JSON or URL. Cookie-required reads and receipt upload use exact-origin credentialed CORS.\n\nAfter receipt submission, show reservation details and ask the guest to screenshot before leaving; confirm with a guard modal. Migration 0070 cancels queued customer email while preserving business notices; old API/worker processes must stop before rollout."}
  ],
